Question: does `-sm layer` across both 3090s give near-single-GPU throughput at
roughly half the per-device VRAM, and does it do so EVENLY? The only VRAM lever
the agent uses today is `-ot ...=CPU`, which spills FFN weights to host RAM and
is measured to cost 58-86% of decode throughput. Layer-splitting should cost
near-nothing, since each GPU computes its own layers and only activations cross
the bus.

Five arms: single/CPU-offload/split at n_ctx 32768, and single/split at the
shipped 81920. `-ts 1,1` is passed explicitly because llama.cpp's default
splits by AVAILABLE VRAM, so a busy card would skew it. `max_minus_min_mib` is
reported as a number rather than asserting "evenly" in prose.

NOT YET RUN -- no results file here, only the plan, arms and harness. It needs
both 3090s idle.

